The bootstrapped Zotero plugin lifecycle and scaffold configuration follow the
public patterns used by Zotero's Make It Red example and
Woif-sha/paper-translate-for-zotero. Changes include the plugin identity,
Zotero 9 compatibility boundary, Reader section lifecycle, and XPI contents.

The recommendation-model provider cards, active-model selection, draft
connection testing, Legacy auth.json transport, and OpenAI Compatible
Chat Completions SSE transport are directly adapted from Paper Translate for
Zotero, Copyright (C) 2026 Woif-sha and contributors, licensed under
AGPL-3.0-or-later and fixed to commit
969f1350a583c45a21303aeba133ab37e488f1af (v1.4.6). The adapted implementation
is renamed for Reference for Zotero, keeps independent preferences, and does
not read Paper Translate configuration or runtime objects. Paper Translate
records llm-for-zotero, Copyright (C) Yile Wang and contributors,
AGPL-3.0-or-later, commit d9724df84ac053343cf32b00c7829620a243e5b9,
as the upstream lineage for the Legacy Codex authentication and provider
transport design; llm-for-zotero is not a second direct implementation source
for this project.

The packaged ScanSci compatibility module contains modified pure-Python
fragments from scansci-pdf, Copyright 2024-2026 scansci-pdf contributors,
licensed under Apache-2.0 and fixed to upstream commit
5e4a6f20ee32b16c0fcb52e37b66ca7a0b31edc5. The upstream commit contains no
NOTICE file. Exact provenance and modifications are recorded in
addon/python/reference_for_zotero_scansci/VENDORED-SOURCE.json and
MODIFICATIONS.md; the Apache-2.0 text is packaged beside the module.
